AsyncTask.execute(Params...) is deprecated in Android 11 (API 30). I currently trigger a custom AsyncTask (Soket_AsyncTask) to SSH into a Raspberry Pi and run a command when a button is pressed. What is the recommended alternative to run this work asynchronously on API 30+ while keeping the SSH approach?

Please provide:
- A brief explanation of why AsyncTask/execute(...) is deprecated in API 30+.
- Updated Android-side code in Java that replaces Soket_AsyncTask/execute() with a modern alternative (e.g., ExecutorService/Thread + Handler, or WorkManager if more appropriate). Show how to invoke it from my onClick and where the network work runs.
- Code that preserves my existing fields (wifiModuleIp, wifiModulePort, CMD) and demonstrates executing the command on the Raspberry Pi over SSH (assume JSch for the SSH client if needed).
- Notes on backward compatibility with older Android versions and any potential issues.
- Any relevant security/best-practice considerations for executing remote commands.

